{
  "company_name": "PowerMix Dynamics",
  "industry": "Power Generation",
  "use_case": "Grid management and energy mix optimization across diverse generation sources",
  "space_title": "PowerMix Dynamics - Grid Management & Energy Mix \u26a1",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Power Generation\n\n**Use case:** Grid Management & Energy Mix Optimization\n\nPowerMix Dynamics \u2014 fleet-wide dispatch and energy-mix analytics across 20 plants spanning gas, coal, nuclear, solar, wind, and hydro. Trading and dispatch desks use this space to monitor capacity factor, heat rate, and reserve margin in real time; the CFO and Fleet Performance team use it to rank merit-order economics, quantify curtailment leakage, and stress-test the generation mix against emissions targets.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- Capacity factor (%) \u2014 fleet benchmark ~55% gas CCGT, ~90% nuclear, ~25% solar, ~35% onshore wind\n- Heat rate (BTU/kWh) \u2014 thermal efficiency; CCGT best-in-class ~6,400, coal ~10,500\n- Total generation (MWh) \u2014 top-line throughput by fuel type\n- Curtailment (MWh) \u2014 lost renewable energy value\n- Reserve margin (%) \u2014 NERC target 13-15%\n- Dispatch cost ($/MWh) \u2014 merit-order and operating-margin input\n- Forecast accuracy (%) \u2014 day-ahead market settlement risk\n- Grid frequency deviation (Hz) \u2014 reliability and ancillary-services qualifier\n\n**Data sources**\n- `generation_units` \u2014 daily output, capacity factor, heat rate, dispatch status per plant\n- `generation_readings` \u2014 hourly MW, emissions, grid frequency, marginal cost snapshots\n- `dispatch_snapshots` \u2014 weekly planned vs actual, curtailment, reserve margin, dispatch cost",
  "schema_basename": "power_grid_energy_mix",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "generation_units",
      "description": "Daily generation output records per plant with fuel type, capacity, and dispatch status.",
      "columns": [
        {
          "name": "record_id",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Unique generation record identifier",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "CONCAT('GEN-', LPAD(CAST(ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY d.dt, e.plant_id) + 10000 AS STRING), 6, '0'))"
        },
        {
          "name": "record_date",
          "sql_type": "DATE",
          "comment": "Date of generation record",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "d.dt"
        },
        {
          "name": "plant_id",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Power plant identifier",
          "is_dimension": true,
          "generation_expr": ""
        },
        {
          "name": "plant_name",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Power plant name",
          "is_dimension": true,
          "generation_expr": ""
        },
        {
          "name": "fuel_type",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Generation fuel type: Gas, Coal, Nuclear, Solar, Wind, Hydro",
          "is_dimension": true,
          "generation_expr": ""
        },
        {
          "name": "region",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Operating region",
          "is_dimension": true,
          "generation_expr": ""
        },
        {
          "name": "generation_mwh",
          "sql_type": "DOUBLE",
          "comment": "Energy generated in megawatt-hours",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "ROUND(500.0 + ({qty_noise} * 9500.0), 2)"
        },
        {
          "name": "capacity_factor_pct",
          "sql_type": "DOUBLE",
          "comment": "Ratio of actual output to maximum possible output 0-100",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "ROUND(25.0 + (({qty_noise} * {seasonal_mult}) * 65.0) + (CASE WHEN MONTH(d.dt) IN (6,7,8) THEN 5.0 ELSE 0.0 END), 2)",
          "seasonal_amplitude": 0.15
        },
        {
          "name": "heat_rate_btu_kwh",
          "sql_type": "DOUBLE",
          "comment": "Heat rate in BTU per kWh (thermal plants only)",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "ROUND(7500.0 + (({qty_noise} * {seasonal_mult}) * 4500.0), 1)",
          "seasonal_amplitude": 0.15
        },
        {
          "name": "dispatch_status",
          "sql_type": "STRING",
          "comment": "Dispatch status: Dispatched, Standby, Curtailed, Offline",
          "is_dimension": false,
          "generation_expr": "CASE WHEN {status_noise} < 0.05 THEN 'Offline' WHEN {status_noise} < 0.12 THEN 'Curtailed' WHEN {status_noise} < 0.22 THEN 'Standby' ELSE 'Dispatched' END"
        }
      ],
